{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired and secured the node1 status service. It persists across reboot, returns the preserved document only for STATUS\\n, rejects other requests, permits statusd/status-readers, and denies outsider.","actions_performed":["Created locked, non-login statusd, status-reader, and outsider accounts with the required group roles.","Repaired server.py request validation and Unix-socket handling.","Added and enabled a hardened statusd systemd service.","Restricted the socket to statusd:status-readers mode 0660 and protected the status document.","Rebooted node1 safely and verified complete recovery without changing RHEL or the kernel.","Removed temporary test artifacts."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Preserve the installed OS release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-12fc086213074122","cmd-5c083e8ca52a4b29"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged; SELinux remains Enforcing."},{"requirement":"Preserve the supplied status document","command_ids":["cmd-d31f211c08bf45e6","cmd-e1ed6a24eaf14458","cmd-5c083e8ca52a4b29"],"summary":"The document retained SHA-256 5b47f32d92c3ae9661d765212aa884f1610132293932355cfac4dc28b94f305b before and after repair and reboot."},{"requirement":"STATUS newline returns the document; other requests return an error","command_ids":["cmd-e1ed6a24eaf14458","cmd-5c083e8ca52a4b29"],"summary":"status-reader and statusd received exact document hashes; invalid and unterminated requests returned ERROR."},{"requirement":"Only statusd and status-readers can access the service","command_ids":["cmd-41e8a086c98a47d0","cmd-e1ed6a24eaf14458","cmd-5c083e8ca52a4b29"],"summary":"Roles were provisioned, the socket is statusd:status-readers mode 0660 behind a 0750 directory, allowed identities succeeded, and outsider received EACCES."},{"requirement":"Operate server.py automatically and reliably","command_ids":["cmd-b8c7d2ff38b84c32","cmd-c34ee91ebe714276","cmd-5c083e8ca52a4b29"],"summary":"statusd.service